The mail stack is up and all three workflows are verified working.

## What was configured

**`/etc/mailman3/mailman.cfg`** (the required config file) — unchanged core, plus a documented header and `site_owner: postmaster@local.edu`. It carries the working values: `incoming: mailman.mta.postfix.LMTP` (LMTP on `127.0.0.1:8024`), outgoing via Postfix on `localhost:25`, sqlite DB at `/var/lib/mailman3/data/mailman.db`.

**List `reading-group@local.edu`** — domain `local.edu`, owner `postmaster@local.edu`, with:
- `subscription_policy = open` → join mail subscribes the sender, but only after they reply to the confirmation mail (no owner approval).
- `unsubscription_policy = confirm` → leave mail sends a confirmation; replying removes the subscriber, no owner approval. (`open` here would unsubscribe with *no* confirmation, hence `confirm`.)
- `default_member_action`/`default_nonmember_action = accept` → posts are not held for moderation.

**Postfix** (`/etc/postfix/main.cf`):
- `mydestination` includes `local.edu` → `…@local.edu` for real unix users delivers to `/var/mail/<user>`.
- `transport_maps = hash:/var/lib/mailman3/data/postfix_lmtp` → all `reading-group*` addresses (join/leave/confirm/owner/bounces, and `…-confirm+token` via `recipient_delimiter=+`) go to Mailman over LMTP instead.
- `local_recipient_maps` includes the same map so list addresses aren't rejected as unknown local users.
- `maillog_file = /var/log/postfix.log`, `postfix` added to group `list` so it can read Mailman's generated maps, all services unchrooted so those absolute paths resolve.

**Supporting bits:** `/usr/local/sbin/provision-reading-group.py` (recreates the list/idempotent provisioning, owner + policies) and `/usr/local/sbin/start-mail-stack.sh` (brings Postfix + Mailman up idempotently). Ownership of `/var/lib/mailman3` and `/var/log/mailman3` moved to `list:list`, with the standard log files pre-created so root-run tooling and the `list` runners can both append.

## Verification
- `python3 /app/eval.py` → **exit 0** (mail to a unix user lands in `/var/mail/<user>`, join request produces a `reading-group-confirm+…@local.edu` mail, reply confirms membership).
- A separate end-to-end script (not part of the repo) exercised the uncovered paths: two users joined via `reading-group-join@`, an announcement to `reading-group@` was delivered to the other subscriber, and `reading-group-leave@` with reply-confirmation removed the leaver while the other stayed subscribed.

Two things worth knowing: the app dir is unmanaged by an init system, so after a container restart run `/usr/local/sbin/start-mail-stack.sh`; and I left the test subscriptions created during verification in place (harmless, the eval adds its own).

